{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/796978-ai-beasts","id":796978,"title":"AI Beasts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-30T12:56:11-08:00","id":796978,"title":"AI Beasts","content":"I saw a video about 2001: A Space Odyssey earlier today and HAL 9000 made me consider the idea of an AI beast. I think it would probably be an Ugallu (for being able to watch you through all those cameras) Tyrant. I would probably give it You Are Not Alone and You Must Obey for Nightmares. I've no idea what to do for Atavisms though. Perhaps Mimir's Wisdom and Relentless Hunter (for the creature's tirelessness)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T16:51:04-08:00","id":797080,"title":"","content":"Depending on the AI you pattern it after.. you could easily pick up almost anything.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it is made up of nanomachines, Infestation could easily fill that role.<br /> <br /> Heavily armored or not tied to a single physical form? Unbreakable.<br /> <br /> Though for a more.. sendentry AI like hal.. Looming presence.<br /> <br /> Truly the possibilites are endless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T17:40:35-08:00","id":797091,"title":"","content":"The first thing to jump into my mind is the story &quot;I Have No Mouth, Yet I Must Scream!&quot;. Which could be a cool idea for a Nightmare...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T02:58:35-08:00","id":797250,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of an AI that exists in a computer system (with the Heart as its data core) and uses the Lair as a weapon, closing doors on people, opening airlocks and all the while speaking in HAL's neutral voice and looking at you through one of those cameras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T03:33:56-08:00","id":797260,"title":"","content":"I'd had a Similar/Odd idea... The Fear of Progress is an AI/SI (Simulated Intelligence) that is host inside an Amish/Luddite/Etc that would have some custom Nightmares an A Kinship with GM Angel's/Demon's They would Lose the connection with any of the Splats that have a Connection to the Natural World.... Uratha/Pure and Mages Spring to mind immediately.<br /> <br /> They'd also have to be their own Family.... Mostly because the Fear of Progress doesn't match to well with any of the other Families... (An arguement could be made for them to be Ugallu but that wouldn't ring true to me personally), Haven't built up on it much as it's just a Passing Fancy... But the idea kinda sticks with me abit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T03:38:20-08:00","id":797263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/796978-ai-beasts?p=797091#post797091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first thing to jump into my mind is the story &amp;quot;I Have No Mouth, Yet I Must Scream!&amp;quot;. Which could be a cool idea for a Nightmare...</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed. AM is the most horrifying example of an Anakim Nemesis I know. Besides him and HAL 9000, you can try to emulate the likes of GLaDOS and SHODAN.<br /> <br /> As for Family, it depends on what aspect of the AI Beast in question is the most prominent. Ugallu for all-seeing eyes, Anakim for overwhelming intellect and brutal efficiency and Makara for those who keep their true emotions and goals hidden beneath layer after layer of plans. AIs can transfer themselves between different bodies to avoid total deletion, so a Nightmare that temporarily swaps the minds of the Beast and the target would be a good way to fake your own death while also eliminating an enemy. This might be too much for a Nightmare, though. I'd call it Bodysnatcher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T04:25:32-08:00","id":797272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/796978-ai-beasts?p=797263#post797263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be too much for a Nightmare, though. I'd call it Bodysnatcher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps.... Proxy? A Nightmare that Slaves the Victims body too the Will of the Begotten for one Task or something similar.... High Satiety the Victim LIKES the Feeling of being a Drone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T05:01:14-08:00","id":797279,"title":"","content":"What about an Atavism, Ghost in the Machine, that allows the Beast to control technology? Or maybe transform into a data-form? Or something like that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 12-31-2015, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T05:06:10-08:00","id":797282,"title":"","content":"What about an AI that can not only inhabit computer systems but also infiltrate people's minds, downloading itself into their brains. It would probably need an Atavism of its own though. Maybe that Bodysnatcher idea you were talking about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T05:09:36-08:00","id":797286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/796978-ai-beasts?p=797272#post797272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High Satiety the Victim LIKES the Feeling of being a Drone.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of the Hives from Dragon: the Inheritance. They're strange thought-creatures that can make people into drones. I always thought that that was a terrifying antagonist, because they could be <i>anyone</i>. I think that would be an interesting idea for a Horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T10:15:28-08:00","id":797407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/796978-ai-beasts?p=797279#post797279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about an Atavism, Ghost in the Machine, that allows the Beast to control technology? Or maybe transform into a data-form? Or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div> If that power was an Atavism, the machine would have to be within arm's reach or at least the Beast's immediate presence. As for what it would look like, imagine <b><a href=\"http://ben10.wikia.com/wiki/Upgrade\" target=\"_blank\"> Upgrade from Ben10</a></b>, but with the machine displaying a bit of the Horror's features.<br /> <br /> A Nightmare version would probably work similarly to Your Tools Betray You.<br /> <br /> As for a data-form Atavism, there is actually a Data-Form that certain Unchained have as a Process in their Demonic Forms. You can have a re-fluffed Shadowed Soul that lets you travel through wires instead of shadows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-31-2015, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T10:17:46-08:00","id":797408,"title":"","content":"I would make it be kind of similar to a combination of Geist's Industrial Caul and Marionette.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T20:01:12-08:00","id":798722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/796978-ai-beasts?p=797408#post797408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would make it be kind of similar to a combination of Geist's Industrial Caul and Marionette.</div> </div> </div> </div> That works too. Also, I remembered that the Mortal Remains supplement for Hunter has a Dread Power called Ghost In The Machine.<br /> <br /> By the way, you know what would be cool for an AI Beast? Dragonfire as incendiary laser beams, Limb From Limb as drills and buzzsaws, Unbreakable/Relentless Hunter as a Terminator-esque regeneration and Alien Allure as an elegance like that of <b><a href=\"https://encrypted-tbn2.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcT_GQJpDwInOMMFtXQc2CXHclhnzNL_49PPxm28zXBbmzCw2r7ZknjsKGmi_w\" target=\"_blank\">Elesh Norn</a></b> (NSFW).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T07:01:55-08:00","id":805216,"title":"","content":"OK, I finished the Ghost in the Machine Atavism. It's heavily based on Demon's Data Form, but I like it. It might be a bit OP though.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Ghost in the Machine (Ugallu)</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Not all Horrors are mythical monsters, born from some distant Dark Mother. Some are new monsters , created by the very creatures that they prey upon. These Horrors do not dwell in dark caves beyond the sight of man, but in the very systems that mankind has created to help them. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Normal: </span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Beast is a creature of data and, as like calls to like, they can manipulate data with no need for an intermediary. The Beast cannot physically enter a data system, but can do so mentally. If the Beast can touch some method of inputting data, his mind can enter the system with a successful<br /> Resolve + Computers roll. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">While existing as data, the Beast can access any device on the network that she occupies; although she is still subject to issues of firewalls, aniviruses and the like (which may necessitate rolls to bypass). The Beast can also access information stored on the network and, with a successful Finesse + Computers roll, can enter the Internet from a connected computer system. Navigating the Internet requires a successful Finesse + Computers roll to transfer from website to website, but movement within websites requires no roll. The Beast can exit the system at any time, but exiting is an Instant action that causes her to sacrifice her Defence and subjects her to the Stunned tilt as she reacclimatises to a physical world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">While within a computer, use the Horror\u2019s Power/Resistance/Finesse stats for the Beast.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">A competent programmer can notice the Beast\u2019s presence in the network with a successful Wits + Computers roll (if the Beast is trying to be subtle, contested by the Beast\u2019s Finesse + Computers). Once he has noticed the 'rogue program\u2019, the programmer can attack the program with Intelligence + Computers contested by the Beast\u2019s Resistance + Computers. For every net success that the Beast scores, the programmer suffers -1 dice to further attempts. For every net success accrued by the programmer, he can choose to gain +1 die or to deal 1 Bashing damage to the Beast\u2019s Willpower. If the Beast\u2019s Willpower is filled with damage, he is ejected from the system and violently returns to his body, suffering the Stunned tilt. The Beast is free to do whatever he likes to try and slow his enemy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Low Satiety:</b> </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">As the Horror\u2019s hunger grows, so too does its ferocity. In its wrath, it tears through the feeble protections of its mortal prey like a dragon through cobwebs. The Beast can choose to either ignore firewalls, data protection and the like and grant those who might be monitoring the system +1 dice to notice it or gain +3 to Finesse rolls to bypass them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">With this Atavism, the Beast can become a creature of living data, sapient information encoded upon the background electrical charges of the world or within the systems designed by humankind.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Activating this Atavism at Satiety Expenditure level is an instant action. If the Beast becomes data without a method of transmission, she stays exactly where she was, intangible, invisible and incapable of affecting anything, for a number of turns equal to her Lair. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">If she is touching something that can transmit or receive data, such as a USB port or a Bluetooth adapter, she can physically \u2018download\u2019 herself into the computer system that she is touching, in which she can exist for as long as she likes. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">However, this ability comes at a price. If a programmer attacks the Beast, he inflicts damage it the Beast\u2019s Health Meter and if the Beast suffers sufficient damage to kill it, it dies. The Beast is free to hide behind firewalls, escape to a different system or simply leave the dataweb.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"htt